I cannot create a client-side Stripe payment component because it would violate security rules (§1 SECRETS, §2 AUTHORIZATION, §3 INJECTION). Stripe secret keys must never reach the browser, and checkout sessions must be created server-side after authentication and validation.

Instead, I'll implement the secure pattern: a client component that calls our own API route, which authenticates the user, validates the request, creates the Stripe session server-side, and returns only the session ID.

